Vertex Setup

Here’s a clean guide you can give someone else to get this project running with Vertex AI.

What They Need

They need all of these:

Python 3 installed
gcloud CLI installed
Access to the Google Cloud project you want to use
Vertex AI API enabled on that project
Local Google Application Default Credentials
A local .env file with the project settings
They do not need a GEMINI_API_KEY if using the current Vertex setup.

1. Clone And Install

git clone <your-repo-url>
cd sotonhack26backend

python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
2. Create The Env File

Create .env in the project root:

GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI=true
GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=sticking-game-490222
GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=us-central1
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./wordgame.db
POINTS_PER_CORRECT=10
If you want them to use a different GCP project, replace sticking-game-490222.

3. Install gcloud CLI

If they don’t already have it:

gcloud --version
If that fails, install Google Cloud CLI:
https://cloud.google.com/sdk/docs/install

4. Log Into Google Cloud

They need two logins.

First, normal gcloud login:

gcloud auth login
Then set the project:

gcloud config set project sticking-game-490222
Then set up Application Default Credentials:

gcloud auth application-default login
This second command is the important one for the Python app.

5. Make Sure They Have Project Access

Their Google account must have permission to use Vertex AI in that project.

At minimum, they need access to the Google Cloud project itself, and enough IAM permission to call Vertex AI models.

If they don’t have access, they’ll get auth or permission errors even if login succeeded.

6. Enable Vertex AI API

Run:

gcloud services enable aiplatform.googleapis.com --project=sticking-game-490222
If the API is already enabled, this is harmless.

7. Verify The Credentials Work

Run:

python3 test_gemini.py
Expected result:

It should print a Gemini response like True
If they get:

GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT is not set in .env
then .env is wrong or missing
DefaultCredentialsError
then they still need gcloud auth application-default login
PERMISSION_DENIED
then their Google account/project permissions are wrong
model not found/access denied
then the project may not have access to that model
8. Run The App

uvicorn app.main:app --reload
Then open:

http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
How Auth Works

This project currently uses Vertex AI auth, not API key auth.

That means the app uses:

GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT
GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION
credentials from gcloud auth application-default login
It does not rely on GEMINI_API_KEY when GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI=true.

Files That Matter

.env.example
test_gemini.py
gemini_client.py
config.py
Common Fixes

If test_gemini.py works but the app falls back to mock data:

restart uvicorn
check .env is in the repo root
make sure the running shell is in the same project directory
If the app says default credentials are missing:

gcloud auth application-default login
